    "help": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "content": "\n**Purpose**\n\nFASTQ info is part of [FASTQ utils](https://github.com/nunofonseca/fastq_utils), a set of Linux utilities to validate and manipulate fastq files.\n\nThe tool checks that the input FASTQ file(s) are well formed and reports the number of reads, the quality encoding and the minimum, maximum and median read lengths. Both uncompressed and gzip-compressed FASTQ files are supported.\n\n-----\n\n**Reading the result**\n\nA file that passes every check produces a report ending in **OK**. If a problem is found - a truncated file, a duplicated read name, an unpaired read in paired-end data, or a quality encoding that cannot be determined - the offending line and the reason are written to the report instead of **OK**.\n\nThe two options disable individual checks: skipping the duplicate read-name check, or accepting a quality encoding that cannot be determined (reported as `NA`). A file that only violates a disabled check is reported as valid.\n    "
    }
  },
